    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93643" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σελην-ίτης</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑ] λίθος,
				ὁ</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>moon</i>-stone, <i>selenite</i>, i.e. foliated
			sulphate of lime, so called because it was supposed to wax and wane
			with the moon, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				5.141
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Procl.
				<u>Sacr.</u>
				p.149
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ Σεληνῖται</span>
			<i>the men in the moon</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>VH</u>
				1.18
			</span></i>: fem. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ίτιδες, γυναῖκες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Herodor.
					21
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>a people of Arcadia</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dionys.
			</span></i> Chalcidensis ap. Sch.<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.264
			</span></i>.</div>
